From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:08:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] viz: drop an overlay candidate's clip that clips nothing

Outside delegated compositing, OverlayCandidateFactory keeps the quad's
clip_rect on every candidate, and bakes it into the display and uv
rects only for required (protected) overlays. Web content always
carries the clip of its window, so a video wholly inside it still
reaches the platform with a clip_rect. WaylandOverlayManager refuses
any candidate with one, so on Wayland without delegated compositing
no ordinary video is promoted: Viz.DisplayCompositor.OverlayStrategy
records kNoStrategyAllFail for every frame.

A clip_rect that contains the candidate's display rect changes no
pixels, so drop it. Clipped candidates are unchanged.
---
 .../viz/service/display/overlay_candidate_factory.cc     | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/components/viz/service/display/overlay_candidate_factory.cc b/components/viz/service/display/overlay_candidate_factory.cc
index d0377af9..92a2b05a 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display/overlay_candidate_factory.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display/overlay_candidate_factory.cc
@@ -451,6 +451,20 @@ OverlayCandidate::CandidateStatus OverlayCandidateFactory::FromDrawQuadResource(
     }
   }
 
+  // A clip that holds the whole candidate clips nothing. Dropping it lets
+  // platforms that cannot clip overlays, Wayland without delegated
+  // compositing, take a video that lies inside the page's clip. At a
+  // fractional scale the display rect can overshoot its clip by a rounding
+  // error, which clips nothing either.
+  if (!context_.is_delegated_context && candidate.clip_rect) {
+    constexpr float kRoundingError = 0.01f;
+    gfx::RectF clip(*candidate.clip_rect);
+    clip.Outset(kRoundingError);
+    if (clip.Contains(OverlayCandidate::DisplayRectInTargetSpace(candidate))) {
+      candidate.clip_rect.reset();
+    }
+  }
+
   candidate.has_mask_filter = !sqs->mask_filter_info.IsEmpty();
 
   // Conditionally set the rounded corners once the candidate's |display_rect|
